183:   <section class="section section--white" aria-label="The Shift to Synthetic Sports Surfaces">
184:     <div class="container product-overview">
185:       <div class="product-overview__text">
186:         <span class="section-eyebrow">The Problem</span>
187:         <h2 class="h2">Why are schools and academies replacing raw concrete courts?</h2>
188:         <span class="section-divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
189:         <p class="snapshot">Bare concrete courts cause severe joint impact injuries, lower back strain, and shin splints. Synthetic court flooring—whether acrylic, PVC, or PP tiles—provides essential point-elastic shock absorption, controlled slip resistance, and certified player safety engineered for the extreme temperature variations of the Indian climate.</p>
190:         <p>Indian sports infrastructure is undergoing a massive upgrade cycle. The days of playing on raw asphalt or hard concrete are over. Modern institutions require certified surfaces that protect athletes and meet international federation standards.</p>
191:         <div class="product-overview__tags" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
192:           <span class="pac-tag">Reduces Joint Stress by 35%</span>
193:           <span class="pac-tag">UV & Weather Resistant</span>
194:           <span class="pac-tag">Federation Standard Pace</span>
195:         </div>
196:       </div>
197:       <div class="product-overview__img">
198:         <img src="/images/hero-synthetic-court.jpg" alt="Modern synthetic sports court showing vibrant lines" loading="lazy" style="border-radius:var(--card-radius); box-shadow:var(--shadow-md);" />
199:       </div>
200:     </div>
201:   </section>
202: 
203:   <!-- ============================================================
204:        TYPES OF FLOORING
205:        ============================================================ -->
206:   <section class="section section--surface" aria-label="Types of Synthetic Court Flooring">
207:     <div class="container">
208:       <div class="section-header reveal">
209:         <h2 class="h2">Types of Synthetic Court Flooring</h2>
210:         <span class="section-divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
211:         <p class="snapshot">We supply and install the three primary categories of synthetic sports surfaces, tailored for indoor and outdoor applications across India. We offer manufacturer-direct pricing with absolutely zero middlemen margins.</p>
212:       </div>
213:       <div class="why-grid">
214:         <div class="why-card reveal">
215:           <div class="why-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">
216:             <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-accent)" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
217:           </div>
218:           <h3 class="why-card__title">Acrylic Court Coatings</h3>
219:           <p>5-layer and 8-layer cushion systems. ITF-certified for tennis and basketball. Ideal for outdoor hard courts providing true ball bounce and UV resistance.</p>
220:           <a href="/products/acrylic-court-systems" style="color:var(--color-primary); font-weight:600; margin-top:1rem; display:inline-block;">Explore Acrylic Systems &rarr;</a>
221:         </div>
222:         <div class="why-card reveal reveal-delay-1">
223:           <div class="why-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">
224:             <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-accent)" stroke-width="2"><rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2" ry="2"/><line x1="3" y1="9" x2="21" y2="9"/><line x1="9" y1="21" x2="9" y2="9"/></svg>
225:           </div>
226:           <h3 class="why-card__title">PVC Vinyl Sports Flooring</h3>
227:           <p>High-density, multi-layer indoor flooring. BWF-compliant for badminton, table tennis, and indoor multi-sport halls. Incredible point-elastic shock absorption.</p>
228:           <a href="/products/badminton-pvc-vinyl-sports-flooring" style="color:var(--color-primary); font-weight:600; margin-top:1rem; display:inline-block;">Explore PVC Vinyl &rarr;</a>
229:         </div>
230:         <div class="why-card reveal reveal-delay-2">
231:           <div class="why-card__icon" aria-hidden="true">
232:             <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-accent)" stroke-width="2"><path d="M4 4h16c1.1 0 2 .9 2 2v12c0 1.1-.9 2-2 2H4c-1.1 0-2-.9-2-2V6c0-1.1.9-2 2-2z"/><line x1="22" y1="12" x2="2" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="22" x2="12" y2="2"/></svg>
233:           </div>
234:           <h3 class="why-card__title">PP Interlocking Tiles</h3>
235:           <p>UV-stabilized copolymer tiles. Excellent for fast outdoor retrofits over existing damaged concrete, providing a self-draining, all-weather playable surface.</p>
236:           <a href="/products/pp-interlocking-tiles" style="color:var(--color-primary); font-weight:600; margin-top:1rem; display:inline-block;">Explore PP Tiles &rarr;</a>
237:         </div>
238:       </div>
239:     </div>
240:   </section>
